\subsection{Depth and brain regions}\label{sec:res-depth}

The dense advantage was largest near the scalp (Fig.~\ref{fig:depth}A): the ratio was << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_ib_10_15_ratio >> << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_ib_10_15_ci >> in the << F.g2_depth_bin_10_15_mm >>~mm bin, << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_ib_25_30_ratio >> << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_ib_25_30_ci >> at << F.g2_depth_bin_25_30_mm >>~mm and << F.g2_depth_dense_vs_combined_ib_35_60_range >> from the << F.g2_depth_bin_35_40_mm >> to the << F.g2_depth_bin_55_60_mm >>~mm bin, every interval above 1. The site-matched array had an equal-SNR depth even with sensor plus brain noise: its intervals lay above 1 down to the << F.rev_db_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci_above1_through_bin >>~mm bin and below 1 from << F.rev_db_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci_below1_from_bin >>~mm. With the room field projected out, the dense array's bin median fell below 1 from << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_proj_median_below1_from_bin >>~mm and the site-matched array's from << F.rev_db_matched_vs_combined_proj_median_below1_from_bin >>~mm, with intervals below 1 only at << F.rev_db_dense_vs_combined_proj_bins_ci_below1 >>~mm and from << F.rev_db_matched_vs_combined_proj_ci_below1_from_bin >>~mm, respectively.

For the dense array, the fall with depth was geometric. It was present with sensor noise alone (Fig.~\ref{fig:depth}A, dotted) and in the peak field itself (Fig.~\ref{fig:depth}B), and brain noise multiplied the ratio by a nearly constant factor in every bin (<< F.g2_brainmult_dense_vs_combined_range >>). For sources << F.g2_depth_bin_10_15_mm >>~mm deep, the dense ratio stayed above 1 under every noise alternative examined. It was << F.wr_cov_s4_dense_depth_10_15_ratio >> under scenario D (point estimate), << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_15_ratio >> << F.rev_ns_sweep_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_15_ci >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz, and << F.rev_ns_joint_all_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_15_ratio >> << F.rev_ns_joint_all_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_depth_10_15_ci >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz with near-skull cortex, a << F.rev_ns_joint_corner_hz >>-Hz corner and cardiac and ocular sources added. On the cortex (Fig.~\ref{fig:maps}), the dense array was ahead almost everywhere, most of all on the lateral convexity.

